---
import { AUTHOR_URL, LICENSE_URL, NOTICES_URL } from '../lib/site';
---

<section id="credits" class="section credits" aria-labelledby="credits-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Credits and notices</p>
    <h2 class="title" id="credits-title">Who made this, and with what.</h2>
    <dl class="list">
      <div>
        <dt>Made by</dt>
        <dd>
          I build KireiManga on my own, as <a href={AUTHOR_URL} rel="noopener">Shironex</a>. Kirei,
          the girl with the glasses, is the project's mascot.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Licence</dt>
        <dd>
          Source available under the <a href={LICENSE_URL} rel="noopener">KireiManga licence</a>:
          free for personal, non-commercial use.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Inside the app</dt>
        <dd>
          Tauri, Rust and React, plus third party code such as UnRAR for CBR archives. The full list
          is in <a href={NOTICES_URL} rel="noopener">THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES</a>.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>This page</dt>
        <dd>
          Built with Astro, three.js and React Three Fiber (MIT). Type is Bricolage Grotesque, Onest,
          Shippori Mincho and JetBrains Mono, all under the SIL Open Font License.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Art</dt>
        <dd>
          Every cover and manga page shown here is fictional art made for the project. The screens
          are captures of the design prototype.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Online services</dt>
        <dd>
          MangaDex and AniList support arrives in 1.1. KireiManga is not affiliated with either, and
          it credits MangaDex and the scanlation groups wherever their work is shown.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .credits {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-block: clamp(64px, 8vw, 112px);
  }
  .title {
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3.4vw, var(--t-5xl));
    max-width: 18ch;
  }
  .list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, 340px), 1fr));
    gap: var(--s-6) var(--s-7);
    margin: var(--s-7) 0 0;
  }
  dt {
    margin-bottom: var(--s-2);
    font: 500 var(--t-xs) / 1.2 var(--f-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg-2);
    font-size: var(--t-md);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  dd a {
    color: var(--fg-1);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
</style>
